---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
const STRATS = [['lww', 'Last write wins (whole cart, by timestamp)'], ['union', 'Vector clocks, then union of items'], ['orReg', 'Add-wins set, quantity is a last-write number'], ['orPn', 'Add-wins set, quantity is a PN-counter']];
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Two devices, one partition, one merge" hint="A phone (A) and a laptop (B) edit the same cart while they cannot reach each other. Pick how the copies are merged and compare the result with the cart the shopper meant to have.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>With <b>last write wins</b> on <b>scenario 4</b>, the cart from the device with the later clock replaces the other one: <b>1 item is lost</b> (pen), <b>1 deleted item comes back</b> (lamp) and <b>1 quantity is wrong</b> (book), and only 1 bookkeeping entry is kept.</li>
    <li>Set the <b>laptop clock to 30 seconds slow</b> (or more): the phone's cart wins instead, and last write wins now loses <b>2 items</b>. The same actions give a different result because of a clock. Switch to <b>vector clocks with union</b>: nothing is lost, but the lamp is back and 2 quantities are wrong.</li>
    <li>Switch to <b>add-wins set with a PN-counter</b>: the merged cart is <b>exactly the intended one</b>. The price is bookkeeping, which grows with every operation: <b>24 entries</b> after 5 operations per device. Turn on <b>drop tombstones after the merge</b> to bring it to 18, and raise the operations to 10 to see it grow.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg scb" data-scb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Merge strategy <select class="pg-in" data-strat>
        {STRATS.map(([v, l], i) => <option value={v} selected={i === 0}>{l}</option>)}
      </select></label>
      <label>Scenario <select class="pg-in" data-seed>
        {[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8].map((n) => <option value={n} selected={n === 4}>Scenario {n}</option>)}
      </select></label>
      <label>Operations per device <input type="range" min="1" max="10" value="5" data-k /> <b data-kval></b></label>
      <label>Laptop clock offset (seconds) <input type="range" min="-60" max="60" step="10" value="0" data-skew /> <b data-skewval></b></label>
      <label class="scb-check"><input type="checkbox" data-gc /> Drop tombstones after the merge</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Phone A saw</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Laptop B saw</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Intended cart</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Merged cart</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b5><h3>Items lost</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o5></span><span class="pg-note" data-n5></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b6><h3>Deleted items that came back</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o6></span><span class="pg-note" data-n6></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b7><h3>Quantities wrong</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o7></span><span class="pg-note" data-n7></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b8><h3>Bookkeeping kept</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o8></span><span class="pg-note" data-n8></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="tw" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All four strategies on this scenario"><table class="cmp">
      <caption class="sr">The same operations merged by each strategy. The chosen strategy is marked.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Strategy</th><th scope="col">Lost</th><th scope="col">Back</th><th scope="col">Wrong</th><th scope="col">Units off</th><th scope="col">Entries</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {STRATS.map(([id, label]) => <tr data-row={id}><th scope="row">{label}</th><td data-c={id + 'L'}></td><td data-c={id + 'B'}></td><td data-c={id + 'W'}></td><td data-c={id + 'U'}></td><td data-c={id + 'M'}></td></tr>)}
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
    <div class="tw long" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Operations on each device, in the order they really happened"><ol class="ops" data-ops></ol></div>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: both devices start from the same cart (book 2, pen 1, lamp 1, tea 1), then cannot reach each other, and each makes the chosen number of seeded operations (add an item, one more, one fewer, remove an item). The intended cart is every unit that a shopper added, unless that same device removed it or took it away after seeing it; a remove never cancels an add made on the other device that it could not see, because keeping an extra item is cheaper than silently dropping one. Last write wins keeps the whole cart of the device whose last write has the later timestamp, after adding the clock offset to the laptop. Vector clocks see that the two versions are concurrent, and the application then keeps every item that either device has, with the larger quantity. The add-wins set gives every add a unique tag, a remove only covers the tags it has seen, and a merge is a union of tags and tombstones. With a last-write number, each item quantity is a register and the later timestamp wins, so the clock offset matters. With a PN-counter each add carries its own quantity and each device counts its own decrements, and a merge takes the larger value of each. Bookkeeping counts the entries kept after the merge: 1 timestamp, 2 version counters, or tags, quantities, tombstones and decrement counters. Dropping tombstones is safe only once every replica has seen the merged state.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style is:global>
  .playground .tw { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .playground .cmp { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font: .82rem ui-monospace, monospace; min-width: 520px; }
  .playground .cmp th, .playground .cmp td { border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 4px 6px; text-align: center; }
  .playground .cmp thead th { background: var(--surface-2); }
  .playground .cmp tbody th { text-align: left; background: var(--surface-2); font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .cmp tr.on th, .playground .cmp tr.on td { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: -2px; }
  .playground .cmp td.bad { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bad) 18%, var(--surface)); color: var(--bad-text); font-weight: 700; }
  .playground .sr { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; }
  .playground .scb-check { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .playground .tw.long { max-height: 14em; overflow-y: auto; }
  .playground .ops { margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 2.4em; font: .8rem ui-monospace, monospace; min-width: 260px; }
  .playground .ops li { white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-scb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const ITEMS = ['book', 'pen', 'lamp', 'tea', 'mug', 'sock', 'cup', 'hat'];
    const START: [string, number][] = [['book', 2], ['pen', 1], ['lamp', 1], ['tea', 1]];
    type Cart = Record<string, number>;
    type Op = { d: 'A' | 'B'; type: string; item: string; q: number; t: number };

    // One replica of an add-wins observed-remove set, with per-tag quantities and a decrement counter per tag.
    class Rep {
      id: string; n: number; tags: Map<string, string>; amount: Map<string, number>; dead: Set<string>; dec: Map<string, number>; reg: Map<string, { v: number; ts: number; by: string }>;
      constructor(id: string, from?: Rep) {
        this.id = id; this.n = from ? from.n : 0;
        this.tags = new Map(from ? from.tags : []); this.amount = new Map(from ? from.amount : []); this.dead = new Set(from ? from.dead : []);
        this.dec = new Map(from ? from.dec : []); this.reg = new Map(from ? from.reg : []);
      }
      left(t: string) { let d = 0; for (const [k, v] of this.dec) if (k.split('|')[0] === t) d += v; return (this.amount.get(t) || 0) - d; }
      live(item: string) { return [...this.tags].filter(([t, i]) => i === item && !this.dead.has(t)).map(([t]) => t); }
      qty(item: string) { return this.live(item).reduce((s, t) => s + this.left(t), 0); }
      setReg(item: string, v: number, ts: number) { this.reg.set(item, { v, ts, by: this.id }); }
      add(item: string, q: number, ts: number) { const had = this.qty(item); const t = `${this.id}#${this.n++}`; this.tags.set(t, item); this.amount.set(t, q); this.setReg(item, had + q, ts); }
      take(item: string, ts: number) { const t = this.live(item).find((x) => this.left(x) > 0)!; const k = `${t}|${this.id}`; this.dec.set(k, (this.dec.get(k) || 0) + 1); this.setReg(item, this.qty(item), ts); }
      remove(item: string) { this.live(item).forEach((t) => this.dead.add(t)); }
      merge(o: Rep) {
        const r = new Rep('M', this);
        o.tags.forEach((v, k) => r.tags.set(k, v)); o.amount.forEach((v, k) => r.amount.set(k, v)); o.dead.forEach((t) => r.dead.add(t));
        o.dec.forEach((v, k) => r.dec.set(k, Math.max(r.dec.get(k) || 0, v)));
        o.reg.forEach((v, k) => { const m = r.reg.get(k); if (!m || v.ts > m.ts || (v.ts === m.ts && v.by > m.by)) r.reg.set(k, v); });
        return r;
      }
      cart(): Cart { const o: Cart = {}; for (const i of [...new Set(this.tags.values())].sort()) { const x = this.qty(i); if (x > 0) o[i] = x; } return o; }
    }

    function scenario(seed: number, K: number) {
      let s = (seed * 7919 + 13) >>> 0; const rnd = () => ((s = (s * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
      const base = new Rep('A'); START.forEach(([i, x]) => base.add(i, x, 0));
      const reps: Record<string, Rep> = { A: new Rep('A', base), B: new Rep('B', base) }; const left: Record<string, number> = { A: K, B: K }; const ops: Op[] = []; let t = 0;
      while (left.A + left.B > 0) {
        const d = (left.A === 0 ? 'B' : left.B === 0 ? 'A' : rnd() < 0.5 ? 'A' : 'B') as 'A' | 'B'; left[d]--; t += 10;
        const r = reps[d]; const present = Object.keys(r.cart()); const x = rnd(); const pick = (a: string[]) => a[Math.floor(rnd() * a.length)];
        let op: Op;
        if (present.length === 0 || x < 0.35) op = { d, type: 'add', item: pick(ITEMS), q: 1, t };
        else if (x < 0.55) op = { d, type: 'more', item: pick(present), q: 1, t };
        else if (x < 0.75) op = { d, type: 'less', item: pick(present), q: 1, t };
        else op = present.length >= 3 ? { d, type: 'remove', item: pick(present), q: 0, t } : { d, type: 'add', item: pick(ITEMS), q: 1, t };
        ops.push(op);
        if (op.type === 'add' || op.type === 'more') r.add(op.item, op.q, t); else if (op.type === 'less') r.take(op.item, t); else r.remove(op.item);
      }
      return { reps, ops };
    }

    // The intended cart is worked out by hand from the operation log, without tags or merging.
    function intended(ops: Op[]): Cart {
      type E = { item: string; q: number; owner: string | null; takes: Record<string, number>; by: Record<string, boolean> };
      const mk = (item: string, q: number, owner: string | null): E => ({ item, q, owner, takes: { A: 0, B: 0 }, by: { A: false, B: false } });
      const ents: E[] = START.map(([i, x]) => mk(i, x, null));
      for (const o of ops) {
        const vis = ents.filter((e) => e.item === o.item && (e.owner === null || e.owner === o.d) && !e.by[o.d]);
        if (o.type === 'add' || o.type === 'more') ents.push(mk(o.item, o.q, o.d));
        else if (o.type === 'less') vis.find((e) => e.q - e.takes[o.d] > 0)!.takes[o.d]++;
        else vis.forEach((e) => (e.by[o.d] = true));
      }
      const out: Cart = {};
      for (const e of ents) if (!e.by.A && !e.by.B) out[e.item] = (out[e.item] || 0) + e.q - e.takes.A - e.takes.B;
      const sorted: Cart = {}; Object.keys(out).sort().forEach((i) => { if (out[i] > 0) sorted[i] = out[i]; });
      return sorted;
    }

    function run(seed: number, K: number, skew: number, gc: boolean) {
      const sc = scenario(seed, K); const want = intended(sc.ops); const A = sc.reps.A; const B = sc.reps.B;
      const clk = (d: string, t: number) => t + (d === 'B' ? skew : 0);
      const lastTs = (d: string) => Math.max(...sc.ops.filter((o) => o.d === d).map((o) => clk(d, o.t)));
      const lww = lastTs('B') > lastTs('A') ? B.cart() : A.cart();
      const union: Cart = {}; for (const c of [A.cart(), B.cart()]) for (const [i, x] of Object.entries(c)) union[i] = Math.max(union[i] || 0, x);
      const skewed = (R: Rep) => { const r = new Rep(R.id, R); r.reg = new Map([...R.reg].map(([k, v]) => [k, { ...v, ts: clk(R.id, v.ts) }])); return r; };
      const m3 = skewed(A).merge(skewed(B)); const live3 = new Set([...m3.tags].filter(([t]) => !m3.dead.has(t)).map(([, i]) => i));
      const orReg: Cart = {}; [...live3].sort().forEach((i) => { const x = m3.reg.get(i)!.v; if (x > 0) orReg[i] = x; });
      const m4 = A.merge(B); const orPn = m4.cart(); const liveT = [...m4.tags].filter(([t]) => !m4.dead.has(t)).map(([t]) => t);
      const meta: Record<string, number> = {
        lww: 1, union: 2,
        orReg: gc ? liveT.length + m3.reg.size : m3.tags.size + m3.dead.size + m3.reg.size,
        orPn: gc ? liveT.length * 2 + [...m4.dec].filter(([k]) => !m4.dead.has(k.split('|')[0])).length : m4.tags.size + m4.amount.size + m4.dead.size + m4.dec.size,
      };
      return { want, carts: { lww, union, orReg, orPn } as Record<string, Cart>, meta, ops: sc.ops, A: A.cart(), B: B.cart() };
    }
    function judge(got: Cart, want: Cart) {
      const lost = Object.keys(want).filter((i) => !(i in got)); const back = Object.keys(got).filter((i) => !(i in want));
      const wrong = Object.keys(got).filter((i) => i in want && got[i] !== want[i]);
      const units = [...new Set([...Object.keys(got), ...Object.keys(want)])].reduce((s, i) => s + Math.abs((got[i] || 0) - (want[i] || 0)), 0);
      return { lost, back, wrong, units };
    }

    const NAMES: Record<string, string> = { lww: 'Last write wins', union: 'Vector clocks with union', orReg: 'Add-wins set with last-write quantities', orPn: 'Add-wins set with a PN-counter' };
    const show = (c: Cart) => (Object.keys(c).length ? Object.entries(c).map(([i, x]) => `${i} x${x}`).join(', ') : '(empty)');
    const names = (a: string[]) => (a.length ? a.join(', ') : 'none');
    const opText = (o: Op, skew: number) => `t=${String(o.t + (o.d === 'B' ? skew : 0)).padStart(4, ' ')} ${o.d === 'A' ? 'phone ' : 'laptop'} ${o.type === 'add' ? `add ${o.item}` : o.type === 'more' ? `one more ${o.item}` : o.type === 'less' ? `one fewer ${o.item}` : `remove ${o.item}`}`;
    const IDS = ['lww', 'union', 'orReg', 'orPn'];
    const rowEls = Object.fromEntries(IDS.map((id) => [id, q<HTMLElement>(`[data-row="${id}"]`)]));
    const cell = (k: string) => q<HTMLElement>(`[data-c="${k}"]`);
    const tint = (n: string, c: string) => q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${n}]`).style.setProperty('--c', c);

    function draw() {
      const strat = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-strat]').value; const seed = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-seed]').value);
      const K = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-k]').value); const skew = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-skew]').value); const gc = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-gc]').checked;
      q('[data-kval]').textContent = String(K); q('[data-skewval]').textContent = `${skew > 0 ? '+' : ''}${skew}`;
      const r = run(seed, K, skew, gc); const got = r.carts[strat]; const j = judge(got, r.want);
      const all = IDS.map((id) => ({ id, j: judge(r.carts[id], r.want) }));
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = show(r.A); q('[data-o2]').textContent = show(r.B); q('[data-o3]').textContent = show(r.want);
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = `${r.ops.length} operations in total`;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = show(got); q('[data-n4]').textContent = NAMES[strat];
      q('[data-o5]').textContent = names(j.lost); q('[data-n5]').textContent = j.lost.length ? 'the shopper added these and they vanished' : 'nothing the shopper added is missing';
      q('[data-o6]').textContent = names(j.back); q('[data-n6]').textContent = j.back.length ? 'removed on one device, but still in the cart' : 'no removed item reappears';
      q('[data-o7]').textContent = j.wrong.length ? j.wrong.map((i) => `${i} ${got[i]} (want ${r.want[i]})`).join(', ') : 'none'; q('[data-n7]').textContent = j.wrong.length ? `${j.units} units off in total` : 'every quantity is right';
      const m = r.meta[strat]; q('[data-o8]').textContent = `${m} entries`;
      const growth = [1, 5, 10].map((k) => run(seed, k, skew, gc).meta[strat]).join(' / ');
      q('[data-n8]').textContent = `at 1 / 5 / 10 operations per device: ${growth}`;
      tint('1', 'var(--accent)'); tint('2', 'var(--accent)'); tint('3', 'var(--good)'); tint('4', j.units === 0 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      tint('5', j.lost.length ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'); tint('6', j.back.length ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'); tint('7', j.wrong.length ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'); tint('8', 'var(--accent)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const bad = j.units > 0; out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      const problems = [j.lost.length ? `${j.lost.length} added ${j.lost.length === 1 ? 'item' : 'items'} lost` : '', j.back.length ? `${j.back.length} unwanted ${j.back.length === 1 ? 'item' : 'items'} back` : '', j.wrong.length ? `${j.wrong.length} wrong ${j.wrong.length === 1 ? 'quantity' : 'quantities'}` : ''].filter(Boolean).join(', ');
      const why: Record<string, string> = {
        lww: 'One whole cart replaced the other, so everything the other device did was thrown away, and the winner depends on the clocks.',
        union: 'Nothing is thrown away, but with no memory of removals the union brings back what the other device deleted, and taking the larger quantity discards every decrease and every concurrent increase.',
        orReg: 'Items are tracked by tags, so adds survive and removes only cover what they saw. A quantity kept as one number still loses a concurrent change, and which one is lost depends on the clocks.',
        orPn: 'Every add has its own tag and quantity and every decrement is counted, so the merge is the cart that the shoppers intended.',
      };
      out.textContent = bad ? `${NAMES[strat]}: ${problems}. ${why[strat]}` : `${NAMES[strat]}: the merged cart is exactly the intended one, using ${m} bookkeeping entries. ${why[strat]}${gc ? ' Tombstones were dropped, which is safe only after every replica has the merged state.' : ''}`;
      all.forEach(({ id, j: jj }) => {
        rowEls[id].classList.toggle('on', id === strat);
        const set = (k: string, n: number) => { const c = cell(id + k); c.textContent = String(n); c.classList.toggle('bad', n > 0 && k !== 'M'); };
        set('L', jj.lost.length); set('B', jj.back.length); set('W', jj.wrong.length); set('U', jj.units); set('M', r.meta[id]);
      });
      const list = q('[data-ops]'); list.replaceChildren(...r.ops.map((o) => { const li = document.createElement('li'); li.textContent = opText(o, skew); return li; }));
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
